# Ninety's own backend (see ../ninety-api) — resolves canonical sports
# events (fixtures, teams, kickoff times) and real linear TV channels via
# its own EPG resolver. Replaced Sportmonks entirely 2026-08-17 (€80/month
# dropped — see docs/THIRD_PARTY.md in ninety-api for the fixture-data
# source that took its place). Point this at your local dev server
# (npm run dev in ninety-api, usually http://localhost:3000) or the
# deployed Railway URL. Production builds fail if this is missing, not HTTPS,
# or contains a path/query/fragment.
VITE_NINETY_API_URL=

# Support metadata sent with pairing. Keep synchronized with config.xml.
VITE_NINETY_APP_VERSION=0.1.0
